      "id": 3583,
      "title": "Instagram: 11 Jul 2025",
      "excerpt": "West Valley College is located in the affluent City of Saratoga, however the student population comes primarily from the more urban San Jose area, many of whom have had negative interactions with police in the past. The campus police department was already making outreach efforts–such as assigning more plain-clothes officers to foot patrol and using poodles instead of more intimidating breeds for K-9 units – however, the new District Public Safety & Community Services Building provided a seminal opportunity to build stronger relationships between campus police and students, staff, and the community. \n\nLPAS was challenged by the West Valley-Mission Community College District to help create a place where different populations can come together and feel physically and psychologically safe. We worked with the District and campus police to develop a new building that unites the warmth and welcoming nature of a community center with the security needs of a police station.\n\nSee the full project at https://www.lpas.com/projects/west-valley-mission-community-college-district-public-safety-community-services-building",
