      "id": 3585,
      "title": "Instagram: 25 Jun 2025",
      "excerpt": "The A.J. is a 345-unit mixed-use community that is the first new development in Sacramento’s “The Railyards”—one of the largest and most ambitious urban infill developments in the nation. The building is named for A.J. Stevens (1833–1888) who was a master mechanic for the Central Pacific and Southern Pacific Railroads and renowned for building “El Gobernador,” the largest locomotive in the world at the time. Aligned with Sacramento’s housing and equity priorities, 20% of the units are designated as affordable housing, ensuring inclusive urban growth.\n\nThe A.J. sets the tone for a transformative new district that will nearly double the size of Sacramento’s urban core. See the full project at https://www.lpas.com/projects/the-a-j--1",
